# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions
**/node_modules/
# testing
/coverage

# next.js
**/.next/
/out/

# Previous bun-built Next output, kept locally as a rollback artifact only.
apps/web/.next.bun-old-*/
# The `next-env.d.ts` ignore above is retained: it is a generated file, so
# ignoring it is correct whether or not Next is currently installed. The
# dependency, the app/ tree and next.config.ts are gone from the repo.

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
#
# `.env*` matches `.env.example` too, which is why the template was advertised
# in .dockerignore (`!.env.example`) but absent from the repo: the negation there
# was inert because the file was never committed in the first place. The negation
# below is what makes it real. Keep this pattern and the .dockerignore one in
# step — they answer the same question for two different mechanisms.
.env*
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# monorepo / turbo
.turbo/
dist/

# MCPedia content — DB is source of truth via MCP API (create_document/update_document)
# Filesystem .md files are auto-generated backups, not tracked in git.
# To edit content: use the MCP create_document/update_document tools (requires x-webhook-secret)
content/**/*.md
!content/**/.gitkeep

# moon task runner cache (generated; contains build outputs)
.moon/cache/

# agent worktrees (created under .claude/worktrees by the Workflow tool)
.claude/

# pg_dump snapshots taken before a schema migration. A backup is a copy of
# production data — it must never be committed, and it is deliberately not
# gitignored silently: the reason is recorded here so the next person does not
# re-add the path.
.db-backups/

# CI's release staging area: a copy of the bundles and SPA dist that the deploy
# job uploads. Build output, derived from files already ignored above, so it is
# never committed — and biome must not reformat the artifact CI is about to ship.
payload/
